{"id":"kenaz","name":"Kenaz","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:kenaz"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Kenaz","text":"Hunter. (1.) One of the sons of Eliphaz, the son of Esau. He became the chief of an Edomitish tribe (Gen. 36:11, 15, 42). (2.) Caleb’s younger brother, and father of Othniel (Josh. 15:17), whose family was of importance in Israel down to the time of David (1 Chr. 27:15). Some think that Othniel (Judg. 1:13), and not Kenaz, was Caleb’s brother. (3.) Caleb’s grandson (1 Chr. 4:15)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7073","lemma":"קְנַז","xlit":"Qᵉnaz","gloss":"Kenaz, the name of an Edomite and of two Israelites","kjv":"Kenaz","count":10,"share":0.83},{"strong":"H6274","lemma":"עׇתְנִיאֵל","xlit":"ʻOthnîyʼêl","gloss":"Othniel, an Israelite","kjv":"Othniel","count":5,"share":0.42},{"strong":"H8487","lemma":"תֵּימָן","xlit":"Têymân","gloss":"Teman, the name of two Edomites, and of the region and d","kjv":"south, Teman","count":5,"share":0.42},{"strong":"H201","lemma":"אוֹמָר","xlit":"ʼÔwmâr","gloss":"Omar, a grandson of Esau","kjv":"Omar","count":3,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H6825","lemma":"צְפוֹ","xlit":"Tsᵉphôw","gloss":"Tsepho or Tsephi, an Idumaean","kjv":"Zephi, Zepho","count":3,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H464","lemma":"אֱלִיפַז","xlit":"ʼĔlîyphaz","gloss":"Eliphaz, the name of one of Job's friends, and of a son","kjv":"Eliphaz","count":3,"share":0.25}],"verses":["Gen.36.11","Gen.36.15","Gen.36.42","Josh.15.17","Judg.1.13","Judg.3.9","Judg.3.11","1Chr.1.36","1Chr.1.53","1Chr.4.13","1Chr.4.0","1Chr.15.0"],"related":[{"id":"othniel","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"omar","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"zepho","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"duke","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.068,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"othniel","type